 "evidence_tier": "executed differential (tier 1), against the OpenMS4 Release C++ build",
 "method": "Two oracle drivers link libOpenMS of the Release install. ../oracle/B6-param-defaults writes, for every DefaultParamHandler class the lane ports, getDefaults() and getParameters() of a default-constructed object through ParamXMLFile (<Name>.defaults.ini), and getParameters() after setParameters with one unknown key, with an empty tree, and with the refused values of the set_* cases, recording each case's stdout (exception name and message), stderr (the source's warnings) and exit code in oracle_outcomes.json. ../oracle/B6-tsg-intensity configures TheoreticalSpectrumGenerator through setParameters with double intensities that f32 cannot represent (b_intensity 0.7, relative_loss_intensity 0.9) and prints every generated peak (m/z %.17g, the float intensity's bits, ion name, charge) to tsg_intensity/<case>.tsv, plus three setParameters/updateMembers_ probes of the chemistry contracts (tsg_intensity/*.stdout.txt and *.after.ini). Every case ran twice, each in a fresh process with a clean environment; both runs agreed byte for byte on stdout, stderr, exit code and every written file (results/differ.txt empty).",
